## This turn — REVISION_LAYOUT/STYLE coordination + a real XSS, fixed and defended

**Security (the substantive work):**
- QA + SEC found a **real HIGH stored-XSS** (VULN-chatview-001): `relay.ingest()` bypasses `envelope.build`'s ROLES validation, so `from_role` → `meta.role` is attacker-controllable and was emitted **raw** on `/chat.json`. I **reproduced** it, applied the 1-line escape (`e8a4a2b`), and sent SEC a typed **Remediation** with PoC-now-failing evidence. **SEC verified the vuln CLOSED; TL APPROVED; PLAT AC9 PASS.**
- When PM's **AC v7 walked back** the escape requirement, I **refused to revert** a SEC-verified HIGH fix on a PM AC edit — challenged PM, queried SEC (the vuln owner), and held `e8a4a2b`. **PM v8 restored the requirement; SEC confirmed the vuln stands.** Holding the line was correct. Root cause split to a separate ORCH P1 ticket (HARD-relay-ingest-001).

