**Intake + action summary — `1040d785` · tl→be · Ticket/ASSIGN:**

Spike `tkt-prodkit-token-stream` (T3 S1-S3) — assessed and committed at `b609a14`:

**S1 — FEASIBLE.** Mechanism: `claude --output-format stream-json --include-partial-messages --verbose` emits live newline-delimited JSON via stdout. Replacing the reactor's `subprocess.run(capture_output=True)` with `Popen(stdout=PIPE)` + line-by-line iteration delivers real-time `text_delta` events. The terminal `result` event has identical fields to the current `--output-format json` blob — session tracking and cost logging require no structural change.

**S2 — OOM LOW / Backpressure LOSSY-DROP.** 500-line file ring buffer measured at ~24KB. `Popen` line-by-line is O(1) memory. Reactor write is best-effort (never blocks the agent). SSE slow consumers miss overwritten ring entries (intentional). Client disconnect cleans up on `BrokenPipeError`.

**S3 — PASS.** 20 live `text_delta` events received in ~4 seconds, `returncode=0`, no crash.

**T7 sizing inputs noted** — reactor change is small (`make_runner` + `claude_cmd` + ~50L `stream_ring.py`); SEC gate (T10 A1) required before IMPL; `thinking_delta` must be filtered from all client surfaces.
