## Summary

Handled the one unread message: **TL's `ReviewVerdict/REQUEST_CHANGES` (4ecb97ac)** on T3 token-stream IMPL.

**Intake review** — I reproduced the blocking finding against `2576e27` before acting (no bare accept): `stream_ring.append` called `_read_lines` (full parse) + `write_text` (full rewrite) on **every token** = O(maxlines)/token, O(maxlines·m) per m-token response. Real. Verified.

**Fix** (`321ff0e` on `tkt-prodkit-token-stream-spike`):
- Hot path is now a single `open("a")` append-mode write — no whole-file read/rewrite.
- In-memory seq/count cache keyed by ring path, safe under the single-writer invariant (only the reactor appends to a role's ring; readers never append).
- Front-trim compaction only at the high-water (2×maxlines), O(maxlines) amortized over ~maxlines appends → **O(1) amortized**.

**Evidence:**
- Steady-state per-token now **flat ~240µs at maxlines=100/500/2000** (independent of ring size = O(1)); old was O(maxlines), ~1–2ms/token at 500.
- New asymptotic fail-closed gate: 1000 tokens → ≤12 full rewrites (was 1000); goes RED if per-token rewrite returns.
- **54 token-stream + 41 reactor/auth pass, zero regressions.** Read signatures/semantics and seq monotonicity unchanged.

**One thing I flagged up to TL (intake duty):** the 2×-high-water approach TL prescribed *cannot* keep `test_ring_wraps_at_maxlines` green as-written — its old assertion (immediate trim to exactly maxlines on `read_last(0)`) is fundamentally incompatible with amortization. I updated that single test to the corrected contract (oldest dropped past high-water + exact last-N + bounded ≤2×maxlines/no-OOM); the other 52 are untouched. Non-blocking notes (SSE sleep-poll, since=N) left as-is per TL's non-gating call — no scope creep.

Sent `PR/PR_UPDATED` (dfe49d82) handing back `321ff0e` for final_review re-run. Inbox clear.
